title: Working Women
new-page: true
view-if: crisis = 0 and congress = 0 and c_women_timer <= 0
on-arrival: c_women_timer = 5; month_actions += 1
frequency: 200
is-card: true
tags: party_affairs

= Working Women

Women won the vote in November, and in the war they kept the factories running. Now the men are back, and the women are being sent home from the munitions works, the trams and the offices. Those who stay are paid a third less for the same work. Many comrades think the women's question can wait until after the revolution.

- @paper: Give Clara Zetkin a women's paper and secretariat.
- @queues: Organise the women in the bread queues.
- @general: Fold women's work into the general work of the party.
- @easy_discard

@paper
subtitle: Costs 1 fund. Women join in the textile towns of Saxony and Thuringia.
choose-if: resources >= 1 and comrade_zetkin = 1 and time >= 3
unavailable-subtitle: [? if comrade_zetkin != 1 or time < 3 : Zetkin is not free to take it on. ?][? if comrade_zetkin = 1 and time >= 3 : We have no funds. ?]
on-arrival: {!
Q.resources -= 1;
Q.district_saxony_members *= 1.1;
Q.district_thuringia_members *= 1.1;
Q.luxemburgist_satisfaction += 4;
!}

Die Kommunistin appears every fortnight. In the mills of Plauen and Gera, whole sewing rooms join at once.

@queues
subtitle: Angry marches on the town halls of Berlin. The police are called.
on-arrival: {!
RG.district('berlin', {militancy: 8, repression: 3});
Q.worker_support += 2;
!}

Hundreds of women march on the town hall of Neukölln with empty baskets. The mayor promises an inquiry, and the women promise to come back.

@general
subtitle: The men in the districts are relieved. Fewer women stay.
on-arrival: {!
Q.unity += 3;
Q.luxemburgist_satisfaction -= 4;
for (var d of Q.districts) {
    Q['district_' + d + '_members'] *= 0.98;
}
!}

The Zentrale decides there is no women's question, only the class question. The women comrades notice who decided it.
